I have been embedding message() statements in my RMD file as notification to myself during the knitting process to see progress and to debug. The messages print to the console to show me progress, and do not print to the document. This is all as I want it.

Near the beginning of my document, I have set the debug level to not display warnings from packages (not sure if this is relevant):
```options(warn=-1)```

Strangely, with this setup, I've found that when I set message=TRUE in a code block, messages will NOT be written to the console during knitting, but if I set it to FALSE, they do print.  Since I found this out, I've just made sure to set it to FALSE everywhere and I get the messages I want. Everything is working fine.

